---
import Page from '../components/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { RUBRIC_VERSION } from '../lib/rubric';
import { CONTENT_LAST_UPDATED } from '../lib/build-metadata';

const toc = [
  { id: 'base', n: 'Versioned base URL' },
  { id: 'endpoints', n: 'Endpoints' },
  { id: 'envelope', n: 'Envelope contract' },
  { id: 'schema', n: 'Schema' },
  { id: 'cache', n: 'Caching' },
  { id: 'license', n: 'License' },
];

const baseUrlExample = `https://defirisk.co/api/${RUBRIC_VERSION}/`;

// Two distinct envelope shapes, kept in sync with the real wire JSON
// (data/api/${RUBRIC_VERSION}/index.json + protocols/aave-v3.json).
//
// index.json: lightweight list, no M1 fields at envelope level or per row.
const indexEnvelopeExample = `{
  "rubric_version": "${RUBRIC_VERSION}",
  "data_as_of": "2026-05-05T12:41:36Z",
  "generated_at": "2026-05-06T22:06:43Z",
  "data": {
    "protocols": [
      {
        "slug": "aave-v3",
        "display_name": "Aave v3",
        "headline_grade": "B",
        "total_value_secured_usd": 14063906193,
        "status": "live",
        "has_active_incident": true
      }
    ]
  }
}`;

// Protocol detail envelope: M1 v4 fields at top-level (canonical) AND
// mirrored under data.protocol_data.protocol.* (back-compat copy).
const envelopeExample = `{
  "rubric_version": "${RUBRIC_VERSION}",
  "data_as_of": "2026-05-17T15:29:57Z",
  "generated_at": "2026-05-18T11:38:41Z",
  "risk_score": 17.09,
  "category_severities": { "1": 5.80, "2": 13.04, "5": 44.44 },
  "cap_applied": "none",
  "cap_reason": null,
  "data": {
    "protocol_data": {
      "protocol": {
        "slug": "aave-v3",
        "display_name": "Aave v3",
        "headline_grade": "B",
        "total_value_secured_usd": 14063906193,
        "risk_score": 17.09,
        "category_severities": { "1": 5.80, "2": 13.04, "5": 44.44 },
        "cap_applied": "none",
        "cap_reason": null
      }
    }
  }
}`;
---

<Page
  pageTitle="Data & API"
  description="All data is open under CC BY 4.0. Adapter code under MIT. Stable JSON envelope."
  crumbs={[{ n: 'Data & API' }]}
  toc={toc}
  hero={{
    h1: 'Data & API',
    lede: 'All data is open under CC BY 4.0. Adapter code under MIT. Stable JSON envelope.',
    meta: [
      { label: 'Base URL', value: `defirisk.co/api/${RUBRIC_VERSION}` },
      { label: 'Schema', value: RUBRIC_VERSION },
      { label: 'License', value: 'CC BY 4.0 · MIT' },
      { label: 'Last updated', value: CONTENT_LAST_UPDATED.data },
    ],
  }}
>
  <h2 id="base">Versioned base URL <a class="alink" href="#base">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    Every endpoint is prefixed by the rubric version. Breaking changes increment the minor
    component (e.g. <code>v1.5.0</code> → <code>v1.6.0</code>); additive changes do not. Older
    version paths are intended to remain available after a new minor is released.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="base URL"
    lang="https"
    code={baseUrlExample}
    copyLabel="Copy base URL example"
  />

  <h2 id="endpoints">Endpoints <a class="alink" href="#endpoints">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    All endpoints return JSON wrapped in the envelope contract. No pagination cursor at v1;
    the dataset is small enough to ship in a single payload per list endpoint.
  </p>

  <div class="endpts">
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/index.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Lightweight protocol index: slug, grade, TVL</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/protocols/&#123;slug&#125;.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Full per-protocol assessment with all factor scores</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/factors.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Rubric factor definitions (all 184)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/factors/&#123;id&#125;.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Methodology + per-protocol scores + linked hacks</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/hacks.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Historical hacks ledger</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/rubric.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Current rubric version + frozen-at timestamp</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ep">
      <span class="verb">GET</span>
      <span class="path">/api/{RUBRIC_VERSION}/changes.json</span>
      <span class="desc">Reverse-chronological grade-change log</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="envelope">Envelope contract <a class="alink" href="#envelope">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    Every successful response is a JSON object stamped with <code>rubric_version</code>,
    <code>data_as_of</code>, and <code>generated_at</code> at the top level, followed by a
    <code>data</code> payload. The stamps make every response self-citing.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    title="protocol detail envelope (with M1 v4 fields)"
    lang="json"
    code={envelopeExample}
    copyLabel="Copy protocol detail envelope example"
  />

  <p style="margin-top:1.5rem">
    The <code>index.json</code> / list envelopes omit the four M1 v4 fields;
    they are protocol-specific and only appear on protocol-detail responses
    and at the envelope top level. List rows are lightweight on purpose:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="index.json envelope (lightweight, no M1 fields)"
    lang="json"
    code={indexEnvelopeExample}
    copyLabel="Copy index JSON envelope example"
  />

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><code>rubric_version</code></strong>: the rubric this response was computed
      against. Grades are only meaningful against a specific rubric version.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>data_as_of</code></strong>: the immutable assessment snapshot timestamp.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>generated_at</code></strong>: when this particular file was produced.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>data</code></strong>: the requested resource. An object keyed by resource
      type (e.g. <code>data.protocols</code>, <code>data.protocol_data</code>); never
      <code>null</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="envelope-m1-fields">M1 rubric fields (v1.7.0+)</h3>
  <p>
    Protocol records include the following additional fields introduced with the M1 v4 rubric:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><code>risk_score</code></strong>: numeric 0–100, rounded to 2 decimal places. A
      core-five-weighted average of per-category severity scores plus a critical-red penalty
      (5 pts per critical red, capped at 15). One critical red blocks A; two or more force D or
      worse; three or more force F. Lower is safer. This is the primary input to the letter-grade
      bands, and core-five caps can lower the final grade further.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>category_severities</code></strong>: <code>Record&lt;string, number&gt;</code>.
      Maps each category id (as a string, e.g. <code>"1"</code>) to its 0–100 severity score.
      Gray factors are excluded from the denominator; 0 means all green or no graded factors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>cap_applied</code></strong>: <code>"none" | "D" | "F"</code>. When a
      core-five category has severity ≥ 60, the grade is capped to D; ≥ 90 caps to F. This
      field records whether a cap was applied.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>cap_reason</code></strong>: human-readable explanation of the cap
      (e.g. <code>"Cat 5 severity 67 ≥ 60 (core-five cap)"</code>), or <code>null</code> when
      <code>cap_applied</code> is <code>"none"</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Callout kind="info" label="Cite the snapshot">
    <p>
      When citing data downstream, attach the <code>data_as_of</code> timestamp and
      <code>rubric_version</code>. A grade is only meaningful against the rubric version under
      which it was computed.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="schema">Schema <a class="alink" href="#schema">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    JSON Schema definitions for every resource type are published alongside the API and versioned
    in lockstep with the rubric. The schema is open under CC BY 4.0; reuse it freely.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    title="schema index"
    lang="https"
    code={`https://defirisk.co/api/${RUBRIC_VERSION}/schema/envelope.json`}
    copyLabel="Copy schema index URL"
  />

  <h2 id="cache">Caching <a class="alink" href="#cache">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    All API responses are static JSON files emitted by the build pipeline and served by the CDN.
    They carry standard HTTP cache headers. New rubric versions live at new paths; old paths are
    immutable.
  </p>

  <h2 id="license">License <a class="alink" href="#license">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    Everything we publish is licensed for unrestricted reuse, subject to attribution. Data is
    <code>CC BY 4.0</code>; code is <code>MIT</code>. Attribution to "DeFi Risk, rubric {RUBRIC_VERSION}" suffices for any data reuse.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Nightly CSV:</strong> Planned; no CSV files are published yet.</p>
</Page>
